<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<metadata>

  <!--
    Three classes are dropped from the binding. Each one is a HARD BUILD ERROR if left
    in, not a preference: the generator emits a C# class that does not satisfy the
    abstract members it inherits, and the compiler rejects it.

      GraphRequestAsyncTask   CS0534: does not implement AsyncTask.DoInBackground.
      FileDownloadTask        CS0534: same, in the app-events internals.
      GraphRequestBatch       CS0534 + CS0115: extends AbstractList without an emittable
                              Size()/Get(int); the generated InvokeSize() overrides nothing.

    Safe to remove because none is reachable from what the app calls. The app uses exactly
    two entry points, FacebookSdk (init + the three consent flags) and AppEventsLogger
    (ActivateApp), and neither takes or returns any of these types. They remain present in
    the shipped .aar and fully usable by Meta's own Java at runtime; only the C# projection
    is suppressed.

    If a future SDK bump reintroduces a CS0534/CS0115 on some other class, extend this list
    the same way rather than reaching for a Java wrapper project.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.facebook']/class[@name='GraphRequestAsyncTask']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.facebook']/class[@name='GraphRequestBatch']" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.facebook.appevents.internal']/class[@name='FileDownloadTask']" />

</metadata>
